inflation in the united states just came  in at a brand new 40-year high the  official number for the month of june is  9.1  according to the cpi this is absolutely  insane in one of the most developed and  one of the largest economies in the  world now if we take a look as to what  is driving this 9.1 percent inflation  number you can see that there's a whole  bunch of chaos underneath it  first fuel oil is up almost 100  over the last 12 months  gasoline is up 60 percent electricity is  up 13.7 percent new cars are up 11.4  transportation of 8.8 used cars up 7  and shelter allegedly is only up 5.6  but the number that jumps out to me here  is none of those it's instead the cost  of eating food at home has increased  more than 12  over the last year that is completely  unsustainable for the average american  family now one of the things that the  inflation numbers tend to hide is that  real wage growth is not growing it's  going down meaning that most people in  the american economy are actually  getting paid less money today than they  were a year or two years ago here's a  great way to look at it we've got this  chart that shows all of the u.s wage  growth since the start of the borrowing  and printing binge has been a mirage up  12.3 percent in nominal terms but it's  actually negative negative 1.5 percent  after adjusting for higher prices as  charlie points out initially everyone  loves free money it's only with the  passage of time that the ravages of  inflation are revealed another way to  think about this is that you may be  getting paid more dollars but those  dollars are worth less in purchasing  power terms it means that you're not  getting a raise fast enough to keep up  with the rising prices so you're  actually in a worse position now the  loose monetary policy and the  undisciplined fiscal policy that the  united states has pursued for the last  two years we mitigated the short-term  pain caused by kovid and the government  lockdowns and all that liquidity crisis  in march and april of 2020 but it was at  the cost of the long-term pain of high  inflation and we now sit with a 40-year  high but there's a word of caution  there's a lot of people who will start  to say that inflation is coming down but  they don't actually understand math  if you look at this chart from heather  long what you can see is that plenty of  people will point to this pink line  which shows core inflation that does not  include food and energy and they'll say  look it's starting to come down but the  problem is as heather points out gas  energy groceries and rent are all rising  sharply and so you can manipulate data  to have that pink line come down but the  blue line that includes everything  including energy and food which is a  staple purchase for every american  family we continue to see inflation  rising now of course when you have math  anyone can manipulate the numbers to say  whatever they want but if you go to the  grocery store you go out to eat if you  try to purchase goods and services in  the economy what you can tell is that  prices are much higher than they've  previously been  and wages are not keeping up pushing  people into further and further dire  situations at the end of the day 9.1  percent inflation in the official  reading is likely inaccurate but if we  go ahead and give them the benefit of  the doubt and we say that inflation  actually is 9.1 percent that's almost  double digits and in a developed country  like the united states of america  which serves as one of the largest  economies in the world  that is absolutely disastrous and so  either they're gonna have to get this  under control or people will continue to  suffer and unfortunately most americans  have no clue what to do with inflation  this high
 

